{"text": " Now the year 2100, that morning has not happened yet, but we can follow the evidence. In 2023, a small Caltech satellite called Maple Beam Power wirelessly in space and aimed a signal at a rooftop in Pasadena. It was tiny, but it worked. In 2014, the International Energy Agency sketched a world where solar could make 27% of all electricity by 2050 and stressed that this was not a forecast. Put those together and here is one scenario. Power collected in orbit where the sun never sets. Cities designed around sunlight. The sun itself will not notice. NASA estimates it has another 5 billion years or so. The question is not whether the sun will be there in 2100. It is what we will have learned to do with it.", "segments": [{"id": 0, "seek": 0, "start": 0.0, "end": 3.32, "text": " Now the year 2100, that morning has not happened yet,", "tokens": [50364, 823, 264, 1064, 5080, 628, 11, 300, 2446, 575, 406, 2011, 1939, 11, 50560], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13484431650036963, "compression_ratio": 1.4792452830188678, "no_speech_prob": 0.014017521403729916, "words": [{"word": " Now", "start": 0.0, "end": 0.2, "probability": 0.8616971373558044}, {"word": " the", "start": 0.2, "end": 0.36, "probability": 0.8781915903091431}, {"word": " year", "start": 0.36, "end": 0.52, "probability": 0.9942635893821716}, {"word": " 2100,", "start": 0.52, "end": 1.32, "probability": 0.8629804849624634}, {"word": " that", "start": 1.74, "end": 1.94, "probability": 0.9961854815483093}, {"word": " morning", "start": 1.94, "end": 2.28, "probability": 0.8974047303199768}, {"word": " has", "start": 2.28, "end": 2.48, "probability": 0.9911884069442749}, {"word": " not", "start": 2.48, "end": 2.68, "probability": 0.9996533393859863}, {"word": " happened", "start": 2.68, "end": 3.02, "probability": 0.9965623021125793}, {"word": " yet,", "start": 3.02, "end": 3.32, "probability": 0.9961544871330261}]}, {"id": 1, "seek": 0, "start": 3.68, "end": 5.3, "text": " but we can follow the ev